uidity is ample (current ratio 2.04)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 14.3% over 3 years, 14.2% over 5 years and 8.0% over 10 years.","At current returns, reinvesting 69% of profits supports about 10.5% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded -5.2% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 1.30 (orders outpacing sales), a backlog worth 1.0x annual revenue and deferred revenue down 7%.","Capex runs 2.6x depreciation (7.3% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 21, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.2%), and institutions hold 92%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (6 sales, net $6.1M sold).","It returns 4.2% a year to shareholders (3.7% in buybacks and 0.4% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 1.5% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 31 consecutive years, raising it 20.7% a year over the last five."],"people":["CEO pay is $4.6M, and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better)."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":61,"head":"Avoid: priced 127% above its fair value of $144.","pros":["Composite 50, above the 39 line (gates 14/26)","Revenue grew 14.2%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA 1.0x","Altman Z in the safe zone","12 analysts' mean target $423 (+30%)"],"cons":["Trades 127% above fair value of $144","P/E 34.4x vs sector 22.1x","EV/EBITDA 24.3x vs sector 12.9x","P/FCF 59.0x vs sector 21.8x"],"flags":["Priced 127% above its fair value of $144"],"need":[],"buy_below":122.5,"vc":{"base":144.12,"base_src":"dcf","bear":89.98,"bull":232.07,"alt_median":81.06,"n_alt":3,"gap":0.7779,"dispersion":0.345,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (34% dispersion)","DCF is 78% above the other models' median ($81.06)"]},"med":{"pe":22.1377,"ev_ebitda":12.904,"pfcf":21.8001,"pb":2.7623,"roic":0.0997,"gro